  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UiO NCHR - Investigative Interviewing in Ukraine: Upholding Human Rights in Law Enforcement and Criminal Justice Governance (2024-2027)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Norwegian Center for Human Rights is cooperating with JustGroup and the Prosecutor General&apos;s Office in Ukraine on efforts to secure better evidence and information from interviews with victims, witnesses, and suspects in criminal cases. Training in investigative interviewing for police investigators and prosecutors in line with the &quot;Principles on Effective Interviewing for Investigations and Information Gathering&quot; (the M&#xe9;ndez Principles) makes up the backbone of the project. A particular emphasis is on investigation of war crimes, but also topics like interviewing of vulnerable persons, including children, investigation of sexual crimes, corruption, and investigative management are core parts of the project. The aim of the cooperation is to ensure that Ukrainian police and prosecution conduct human rights compliant, effective, and reliable investigations and apply methods that are founded in science and ethics.</narrative>
  </description>
